exports[`scan a photo: saved, figures filled (Wholesale), checks against total and date 3`] = `
## prompt
This is a photo of the last page of a South African retail till cash-up / Z-report (amounts in Rand) for the Wholesale department of a factory shop.
Read the TOTAL amount per payment/tender type as printed on the report. Map tenders to these keys:
- cash: Cash (notes and coins tender)
- cashguard: CashGuard (cash recycler / CashGuard tender)
- card: Credit card / debit card / speedpoint / card machine totals combined
- cardcbm: Credit card CBM (the CBM card machine; keep separate from card)
- payfast: PayFast card payments (keep these separate from card)
- eft: EFT / bank transfer
- shop2shop: Shop2Shop
- snapscan: SnapScan
Return ONLY JSON: {"cash":number|null,"cashguard":number|null,"card":number|null,"cardcbm":number|null,"payfast":number|null,"eft":number|null,"shop2shop":number|null,"snapscan":number|null,"total":number|null,"date":"YYYY-MM-DD"|null,"readable":true|false}
Use null when a tender is not on the report. Give amounts as plain JSON numbers with a dot for decimals (e.g. 1234.56), without currency symbols, spaces or thousands separators, even if the slip prints them as "R 1 234,56". Set readable false if the photo is not a cash-up report or too blurry to read.
`;

